...and yes, a specific situation that is more likely than others to cause issues is when the inout points are too regular, which seems to be the case for you. Try nudging your boundary specification point a little bit (randomly with size of order 1e-4 may be enough). The underlying issue is that floating point arithmetic leads to difficult to detect inconsistencies in the numerics for the messing algorithm.

Finn

